	(descr "ECS-TXO-5032-122.8-TR, 12.288 MHz HCMOS TCXO, 3.3V, 5.0x3.2mm 4-pad SMD -- real vendor footprint/pinout, converted from lib/ECS-TXO-5032-122.8-TR/OSC_ECS-TXO-5032-122.8-TR.kicad_mod (SnapEDA, sourced from ECS's own mechanical drawing). Pin 1 = N/C (VCONT on the VC-TCXO variant only -- this part is the plain TXO, so pin 1 is genuinely unused), pin 2 = GND, pin 3 = Output, pin 4 = VDD, per ecsxtal.com/store/pdf/ECS-TXO-5032.pdf p.2. The vendor STEP's native orientation has the part lying on its long-axis side rather than flat -- needs a -90deg X rotation (no offset) to sit right-side-up, centered on the pads; verified visually (top/front/iso renders) since no alignment info was given in the datasheet. Re-check if the STEP file is ever replaced.")
